        "PMC8346963::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al diffusion and oxidation are sufficiently synchronized with those of Cr.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Si diffusion and oxidation are sufficiently synchronized with those of Cr.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Synchronization of Cr and X transport promotes a continuous, interpenetrating X-oxide/chromia network.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9498035::web::011::3_1_oxidation_of_the_equiatomic_alcocrfe"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A continuous interpenetrating oxide network causes the scale to remain coherent, adherent, and protective.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9498035::web::011::3_1_oxidation_of_the_equiatomic_alcocrfe"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mn diffuses more rapidly than Cr during high-temperature oxidation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A Cr/Mn kinetic mismatch produces compositionally heterogeneous oxide layers.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::web::028::4_3_oxidation_in_air"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Compositionally heterogeneous Mn-bearing oxides accumulate stress and consequently crack or spall.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8346963::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant structural mediator is a density-graded scale with an inner Cr-rich layer intermixed with X-derived oxide.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide/substrate interfacial structure mediates scale adhesion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "CrFeCoNiAl forms both alumina and chromia during high-temperature oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9498035::web::011::3_1_oxidation_of_the_equiatomic_alcocrfe"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "CrFeCoNiSi undergoes interlinked growth of silica and chromia.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "CrFeCoNiAl will form a stable, adherent, continuous protective scale.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9498035::web::011::3_1_oxidation_of_the_equiatomic_alcocrfe"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
